{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I’m Dr. Lee, one of the hospitalists. You were brought in this morning for nausea, vomiting, and high blood sugar. Can you tell me what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes… I ate potato salad and meat last night, and by bedtime I felt nauseous. I had two loose stools. This morning I threw up and my blood sugar was 600 in the ambulance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve had this before. Were you able to keep anything down after vomiting?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:34:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, not really. I took Zofran but it didn’t help much. I got scared and called the ambulance."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:35:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That was the right call. Your blood sugar was very high—627 when you arrived—but you’re not in diabetic ketoacidosis, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:36:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not DKA? I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, your labs show no acidosis. We gave you IV insulin to bring it down. We also gave Zofran and Dilaudid for nausea and discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:39:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My stomach still feels off, but the pain is better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:40:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your exam shows no serious abdominal issues. Lungs are clear, heart normal. We did a chest X-ray to check for infection—it’s fine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:42:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been having a lot of back pain too, since my car accident years ago."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:43:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, I see you’re on gabapentin and Tylenol. We’ll continue those. No point tenderness in your back, so no new injury."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:44:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my diabetes… it’s always so hard to control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2125-06-20 08:45:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll talk more about that. For now, we’re starting you on fluids and will try to get you on a regular diet later today if you’re stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2125-06-20 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. You’ve been doing well—no vomiting, and you kept down some crackers. We’re going to advance you to a regular diabetic diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2125-06-20 12:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I was worried I’d throw it up again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2125-06-20 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor closely. Your blood sugar was high earlier after ice chips—did you know they have sugar in them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2125-06-20 12:19:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, I didn’t! I thought it was just water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2125-06-20 12:20:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a common mistake. We’ll go over diet counseling to help avoid surprises like that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood work came back. Your kidney function was a bit off when you arrived—creatinine 1.2—but it’s improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that from my diabetes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it suggests early diabetic nephropathy. But staying hydrated and controlling your sugar helps protect your kidneys."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t know my kidneys were involved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s stage I, so very early. But it’s another reason to focus on tight glucose control."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been trying… but my sugars swing so much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We noticed. You had a low sugar this morning—down to 60—after treating a high with too much insulin overnight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I just wanted it to come down fast… I get so anxious when it’s high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:10:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. That’s actually something we want to talk about—your anxiety and how it affects your symptoms."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:11:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Sometimes the nausea feels like it’s from panic, not my stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:12:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Psychiatry saw you and thinks some episodes may be linked to anxiety ‘flooding,’ but this time, your symptoms may have been from food or high sugar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So not all of it is in my head?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:15:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not at all. We did a gastric emptying study yesterday—it was normal. So it’s not gastroparesis this time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:16:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that test before and it was normal too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2125-06-21 09:17:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. So we’re focusing on diabetes control and possible gastroenteritis from the potato salad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2125-06-21 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood cultures came back—no infection. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2125-06-21 14:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I didn’t have a blood infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2125-06-21 14:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No. Your symptoms weren’t from sepsis. We’re confident it’s related to your diabetes and possibly the food you ate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2125-06-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We got your A1C result—it’s 12.8%. That means your average sugar has been very high, around 321 mg/dL."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2125-06-22 10:01:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s worse than I thought."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2125-06-22 10:02:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We consulted diabetes management. They recommend keeping your Lantus at 28 units at night, but adjusting how you count carbs."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2125-06-22 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I thought I was doing it right."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2125-06-22 10:05:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You are trying, but we’re changing your ratio to 1 unit of Humalog for every 12 grams of carbs—was it 1:10 before?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2125-06-22 10:06:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I think so. And the sliding scale?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2125-06-22 10:07:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take 1 unit of Humalog for every 40 points your sugar is above 140. We’ll give you a chart to follow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2125-06-22 10:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s different. I’ll need to write it down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2125-06-22 10:10:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and keep a log of your finger sticks. It’ll help your new doctor see patterns."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2125-06-22 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ve set up a lot for you before discharge tomorrow. You’ll see a new primary care provider in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2125-06-22 14:31:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve missed a lot of appointments before… I feel bad about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2125-06-22 14:32:45",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We know. That’s why a social worker will go with you to your first visit. They’ll help you connect with a therapist too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2125-06-22 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That would really help. I want to do better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2125-06-22 14:35:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great to hear. You also have a GI follow-up to repeat an endoscopy for your stomach varices and check if H. pylori is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well—no nausea, eating normally, sugars stable. We’re discharging you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel much better. What about my meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:02:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue Lantus 28 units at night, Humalog with meals using the new ratio. Gabapentin is now 200 mg three times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:03:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It was 200 mg every 8 hours before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Same total dose—just adjusted for easier timing. We’re also adding Zofran as a backup for nausea, but try Ativan first if anxiety is involved."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:06:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:07:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pharmacy has your insulin and supplies. Keep checking your sugars and write them down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:08:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. And I’ll go to the appointments—I promise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to support you. Call if your sugar is very high or low, or if vomiting returns. Otherwise, we’ll see how you do at follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:11:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2125-06-23 08:12:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and good luck with your new care team."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2125-06-20 08:27:00",
    "admission_end": "2125-06-23 11:57:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes, chronic back pain, and anxiety was admitted for recurrent nausea, vomiting, and hyperglycemia after eating contaminated food. Her blood glucose was 627 on admission but not in DKA. She improved with IV fluids, insulin, and antiemetics, and tolerated a regular diet without further vomiting. A gastric emptying study was normal, and blood cultures showed no infection. Her A1C was elevated at 12.8%, prompting adjustment of her insulin regimen to 28 units Lantus at bedtime and a revised carb-to-insulin ratio of 1:12 with correction scale of 1 unit Humalog per 40 points above 140. She expressed motivation to improve adherence and was connected with a new primary care provider, social work, and GI follow-up for esophageal varices and H. pylori eradication. She was discharged home in stable condition with updated medications and close outpatient support planned.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Acute kidney failure, unspecified",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Diabetes with other specified manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Esophageal varices without mention of bleeding",
      "Nausea with vomiting",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Nephritis and nephropathy, not specified as acute or chronic, in diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Diabetes with ophthalmic manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Background diabetic retinopathy",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Diarrhea",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Lumbago",
      "Posttraumatic stress disorder",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health",
      "Dysthymic disorder"
    ]
  }
}
